# Car Scanner upload from the phone

A Termux job uploads new Car Scanner recordings (`.brc`) to `https://files.{{ site.url }}/car/`
every 15 min on unmetered Wi-Fi. `car_ingest` on websvcs imports them into Grafana's Car
dashboard.

- Car Scanner writes a recording when the adapter disconnects or recording stops
- It records only the open screen's sensors: keep a screen with the Car dashboard's sensors open
  while driving
- Uploads need pve2 up; a failed upload retries on the next run

## Access

- Android 11+ hides `Android/data` from Termux; Shizuku's `rish` reads it as the `shell` user
- Without root, Shizuku needs a restart over wireless debugging after every reboot
- The script signs in to Authelia as LLDAP user `car_uploader` with HTTP Basic (one factor)
  - Authelia allows it only `PUT`/`POST` under `files.{{ site.url }}/car/`
  - copyparty gives it write-only `/car`: no listing, downloads, moves or deletes
  - Three wrong passwords in two minutes ban it for five minutes
- A leaked password allows uploads into `/car`, nothing more

## Setup

- LLDAP (<https://ldap.{{ site.url }}>): create `car_uploader`, password from
  `openssl rand -base64 32`
  - Add it to no group: `authelia_gen_access` would open every subdomain to it
- Phone apps
  - F-Droid: Termux and Termux:API (the Play Store builds are outdated)
  - Shizuku (Play Store or GitHub): pair once in Developer options >> Wireless debugging, then
    Start via Wireless debugging
  - Shizuku >> Use Shizuku in terminal apps >> Export files, to `Download/rish`
- Workstation: render (`tools/render_src.sh /tmp/homelab-rendered`, [mac guide](mac_personal.md))
  and copy `src/services/copyparty/termux/{car_upload,car_upload_setup}.sh` to the phone's
  Download folder (`adb push`)
- Termux: the setup asks for the password; allow Termux in Shizuku's prompt

  ```bash
  termux-setup-storage
  bash ~/storage/downloads/car_upload_setup.sh
  ```

- Optional: skip recordings already on the phone

  ```bash
  ~/bin/rish -c 'ls /sdcard/Android/data/com.ovz.carscanner/files/records' | grep '\.brc$' \
    >> ~/.car_upload/sent
  ```

- Optional, Tasker and Termux:Tasker: run `~/bin/car_upload.sh` when Bluetooth disconnects from
  the vLinker

## Test

- `~/bin/car_upload.sh`: new recordings land in `/var/opt/copyparty/data/car/` on websvcs, their
  names in `~/.car_upload/sent`
- Wrong password in `~/.car_upload/netrc`: `401`
- `curl --netrc-file ~/.car_upload/netrc https://files.{{ site.url }}/car/` (a `GET`): `403`
- Notification "rish failed": Shizuku isn't running; start it again

## Fallback without Shizuku

- Car Scanner >> recordings >> press and hold >> Share >> BRC >> Termux >> Edit
- The same script uploads the shared copy and deletes it; on failure it stays in `~/downloads`
